# The Role of Personality Temperament and Student Learning in Principles of Economics: Further Evidence.

**Authors:** Ziegert, Andrea L.

## Abstract
Explores the relationship between student personality types and measures of student performance in principles of microeconomics using the Keirsey Sorter, a 70-question Myers-Briggs Type Indicator (MBTI); results from the Test of Understanding of College Economics (TUCE); and course grades. Suggests that personality types do affect student performance in economics. (CMK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ651313

